        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow%2C_Idaho",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Moscow’s name comes from a town that was itself named after Russia’s capital, not directly from the Russian city.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.blotmagazine.com/2025/11/16/history-of-moscow/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The University of Idaho started a jazz festival in 1967 that evolved into the Lionel Hampton Jazz Festival after his death in 1985.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.blotmagazine.com/2025/11/16/history-of-moscow/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "North of campus, Ghormley Park honors Admiral Robert Ghormley, who hosted the city’s outdoor swimming pool from 1933 to 1997.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
